# --- .astro formatting is DEFERRED until after cutover -----------------------------
#
# Two separate problems, neither worth solving mid-migration:
#
# 1. prettier-plugin-astro corrupts Alpine's dot-modifier attributes when the element
#    sits inside a JSX expression block: it rewrites `x-intersect.once="…"` to
#    `x-intersectωP_once="…"` and then fails to parse its own output. Affects
#    Header.astro and pages/talks/index.astro, which use it inside `{ cond && (…) }`
#    and `.map(…)`. The attribute is fine in plain markup, so it is a plugin bug.
#
# 2. prettier-plugin-tailwindcss re-sorts the utility classes, which changes the
#    class order in the emitted HTML. Rendering is unaffected (utility order in the
#    attribute has no bearing on specificity), but it breaks byte comparison against
#    the Kirby baseline — and scripts/parity.mjs is the safety net for this whole
#    migration. Degrading it for cosmetics is the wrong trade while it still matters.
#
# Run `pnpm prettier --write "src/**/*.astro"` once the baseline is retired, and
# expect a large but semantically empty diff.
src/**/*.astro
